You can just inspect the R-squared from the result of the efaUnrotate funciton. For example,

unrotated <- efaUnrotate(HolzingerSwineford1939, nf=3, varList=paste0("x", 1:9), estimator="mlr")
inspect(unrorated, "rsquare")

The rotation will not change the communalities.

Sunthud

