> Thank you for the suggestion. Most of the syntax works. A slight bug at the level of the intercepts because there is no rhs.

Oh yeah.  Again, there might be a more clever way to do this, but try this:

E.coefs <- parameterEstimates(fit)
E.coefs
C.syntax <- ""

for (i in 1:nrow(E.coefs)) {
  if (E.coefs$op[i] == "~1") {
    C.syntax <- c(C.syntax, paste0(E.coefs$lhs[i], " ~ ", E.coefs$est[i], "*1"))
  } else {
    C.syntax <- c(C.syntax, paste0(E.coefs$lhs[i], E.coefs$op[i],
                                   E.coefs$est[i], "*", E.coefs$rhs[i]))
  }
}
C.syntax <- paste(C.syntax, collapse = "\n")
cat(C.syntax)

> More important, how do you include this in a loop ? While it is already very helpful to have the syntax and to just copy it in the model command, I still need to repeat the operation 100 times in a loop.

 I'm still unsure from your description exactly what it is that you are doing 100 times.  Are there 100 data sets, or is this some kind of iterative procedure?  The above code shows you what a for loop looks like in R, so perhaps you can figure out how to do what you need from that, or it could at least help you make an example of the for-loop you want to execute.

Terry

