I only used the cat() function to print the syntax to the screen so you could see what was saved as C.syntax.  You don't need to save it to a file and then reload it into another object.  Just use C.syntax as the model argument to cfa.

C.syntax <- paste(C.syntax, collapse = "\n")

C.predict <- cfa(C.syntax, data = C.data, orthogonal = TRUE, missing = "fiml", estimator = "MLR")

I'm not sure what caused the errors in your later message.

Terry

